{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785007836,"nonce":"uar6+xHRfjQh4wXky+CLF4zwi9Y=","title":"helm: chart cannot configure OAuth login — real authn is undeployable","message":"`grep -ri oauth deploy/helm/` is empty. The chart's configmap (deploy/helm/scarab/templates/configmap.yaml:24) only ever sets SCARAB_DEV_INSECURE, and never the SCARAB_OAUTH_* five-tuple that config.rs:532 requires.\n\nConsequence: a chart-deployed Scarab can ONLY boot dev-insecure (every caller a synthetic Owner, lib.rs:4783) or refuse to boot (config.rs:576 NoAuthenticator). ADR-0049 authn is implemented in the server but unreachable via the distribution chart.\n\nFix: values.yaml `scarab.oauth` block (clientId/authorizeUrl/tokenUrl/userinfoUrl/scopes/owners) + client secret via an existing-Secret ref (never plaintext in values), wired into the configmap/deployment env. Chart should also refuse the dev-insecure + oauth combination or make precedence explicit.\n\nBlocks any real IdP, including a Dex broker.","files":null}]}